# SLSA-2 Compliance Rules

## Core Principle

Achieve SLSA Level 2 compliance for all CI/CD pipelines. This ensures version-controlled source, hosted builds, and authenticated provenance, eliminating "built-on-laptop" drift.

## SLSA Level 2 Requirements

### 1. Version Controlled Source

- ✅ All source code in version control
- ✅ All changes tracked in VCS history
- ✅ No manual modifications to build artifacts

### 2. Hosted Builds

- ✅ All builds run in hosted CI/CD environment
- ✅ No builds on developer laptops
- ✅ Builds run in isolated, ephemeral environments

### 3. Authenticated Provenance

- ✅ Generate build attestations (provenance)
- ✅ Sign attestations with cryptographic keys
- ✅ Store attestations in tamper-proof system
- ✅ Verify attestations before deployment

## Implementation Checklist

### Version Control

- [ ] All source code in Git repository
- [ ] No manual file uploads to deployment systems
- [ ] All configuration files version controlled
- [ ] Commit history shows all changes

### Build Environment

- [ ] Use hosted CI/CD (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc.)
- [ ] Builds run in isolated containers/environments
- [ ] No local builds for production artifacts
- [ ] Build environment is reproducible

### Provenance Generation

- [ ] Generate build attestations for all artifacts
- [ ] Include build metadata (source commit, build time, builder ID)
- [ ] Sign attestations using Sigstore/Cosign
- [ ] Store attestations alongside artifacts

### Artifact Storage

- [ ] Store artifacts in secure, versioned registry
- [ ] Tag artifacts with provenance
- [ ] Verify provenance before pulling artifacts
- [ ] Use content-addressable storage when possible

## Tools & Standards

### Provenance Generation

- **Tekton Chains**: Kubernetes-native provenance generation
- **Sigstore/Cosign**: Signing and verification
- **SLSA Provenance Format**: Standard attestation format

### Example: GitHub Actions with SLSA

```yaml
name: Build and Attest

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      
      - name: Build artifact
        run: |
          npm ci
          npm run build
          
      - name: Generate provenance
        uses: slsa-framework/github-actions-demo@v1.4.0
        with:
          artifact-path: dist/
          
      - name: Upload artifacts
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3
        with:
          name: artifacts
          path: dist/
```

## Build Security

### Secrets Management

- Use secret management (GitHub Secrets, Vault)
- Never hardcode secrets in workflows
- Rotate secrets regularly
- Use least-privilege access

### Build Isolation

- Run builds in isolated containers
- Use minimal base images
- Remove unnecessary dependencies
- Scan for vulnerabilities

## DO

- ✅ Use hosted CI/CD for all builds
- ✅ Generate and sign provenance for artifacts
- ✅ Verify provenance before deployment
- ✅ Store all source code in version control
- ✅ Use ephemeral build environments
- ✅ Implement build reproducibility

## DON'T

- ❌ Build production artifacts locally
- ❌ Skip provenance generation
- ❌ Deploy unsigned artifacts
- ❌ Store secrets in code
- ❌ Use long-lived build credentials
- ❌ Allow manual artifact uploads

## Verification

### Pre-Deployment Checks

```bash
# Verify provenance signature
cosign verify-attestation \
  --type slsaprovenance \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  artifact@sha256:abc123

# Verify build metadata
slsa-verifier verify-artifact \
  --provenance-path provenance.json \
  --source-uri github.com/org/repo \
  artifact.bin
```

## Compliance Evidence

Maintain evidence for audits:

- Build logs showing hosted execution
- Provenance attestations
- Signed artifacts
- Source code commit history
- Deployment verification logs

## Testing

- Test provenance generation
- Verify attestation signatures
- Test provenance verification
- Verify no local builds in production path
- Test build reproducibility
